{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/789823-things-we-ve-learned-about-c20-from-the-ama-today","id":789823,"title":"Things we've learned about C20 from the AMA today","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-20T10:50:22-08:00","id":789823,"title":"Things we've learned about C20 from the AMA today","content":"I'm just pulling all the C20 related answers together because I like lists for reference. :P<br /> <br /> The AMA is here: <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/rpg/comments/3xldx5/hi_its_onyx_path_back_again_ask_us_anything/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.reddit.com/r/rpg/comment...k_us_anything/</a><br /> <br /> 1. 'In Dark Ages Fae, Unleashing was a way to use magic that sacrificed control for power. In CtD20, it works kinda the same way; you Unleash an Art rather than focusing it through a cantrip. (Expect a KS update on this sometime next week or the week after.)'<br /> <br /> 2. 'The metaplot - including the disappearance of High King David - gets addressed and expanded. I'm not quite ready to go into a great deal of detail just yet, but making sure that the game is accessible to new motleys and that the content is updated for the current year is important to us.'<br /> <br /> 3. 'The book is in redlines right now. Expect to start seeing excerpts this week, but I don't think there will be a full draft up before the end of the KS. Timing just didn't work out that way this time.'<br /> <br /> 4. 'Arts got a bit of revision, so you will be seeing all of the ones from the core, plus a bunch from supplements, plus some new ones.'<br /> <br /> 5. 'Inanimae, hsien, adhene, nunnehi, and the other Gallain get smaller, condensed write-ups, but they're in there!' A Book of Gallain? 'Future books haven't really been planned, but it's by no means impossible.'<br /> <br /> 6. More House Martial arts? 'I don't think there's anything like that in the book, but that's an interesting idea!'<br /> <br /> 7. C20: Since the Sidhe have been around since the mid 60s, have they been around long enough to develop an Affinity realm? 'Some sidhe have.'<br /> <br /> 8. The Changeling Way: Will there be an expanded section on what it actually is, how it functions, etc. How can the Sidhe go through with it? Is it known the Sidhe don't come back? 'That sidhe issue is something I definitely want to clarify a bit, yes. Even if the answer is &quot;the kithain just aren't sure,&quot; the process needs to be explained a little more clearly.'<br /> <br /> 9. 'Here's the pooka frailty as it stands now in C20:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Untruths: Perhaps the greatest con the pooka have pulled is making everyone believe that they never tell the truth. Under most circumstances a pooka can speak the truth as long as its mixed with lies, half-truths, and exaggerations. The trouble comes when a pooka is asked a direct question. A pooka who is asked a direct question must answer with a falsehood. If he wishes to answer truthfully he must make a Willpower roll (difficulty 8) and spend a point of Willpower. </div> </div> </div>'Now, we're playtesting, so we'll see how it works in play.'<br /> <br /> 10. 'I'm restricting playtesting to authors and their groups only, at least for now. If I open things up to volunteers, there will be an announcement on the OPP site.'<br /> <br /> 11. Selkies excerpt: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sailors and dreams of lost loves and broken hearts and all of those who have lost a loved one to the sea gave birth to the selkie. The sea gives and the sea takes away. Anyone who has lived along the coast can attest to the wonders the sea gives to us: delicious seafood, beautiful shells, the delights of swimming and sailing. But the sea is fickle, and where one day it gives us pleasure, the next it drowns a loved one or sends terrible waves that destroy homes and property. Those who truly love the sea describe an inexorable pull that pulls them back just as surely as the undertow pulls under the unwary swimmer. </div> </div> </div>12. Are we looking to see changes to Legacies? 'Haven't gotten as far as Legacies yet, but I do believe we have some new ones.'<br /> <br /> 13. 'Dark-kin do indeed get rules in C20, and I'll be on the lookout for some quick-n-dirty advice on using them in chronicles.'<br /> <br /> 14. 'Any changeling can build with chimera, nockers are just better at it.'<br /> <br /> 15. With the clever borrowing from Dark Ages Fae of unleashing, are there other portions of DA:Fae you liked enough to consider applying to the new product? 'Some of the history sneaks in there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />'<br /> <br /> 16. We're going to see material, thanks to Kickstarter milestones achieved, for creating kiths. Will this be storied in some way? For example, might we see a kithain analog to Vampire Caitiff and where they may fit into the social dynamic of the courts and long-running kiths? 'Don't know yet! That section isn't written, and I haven't started to talk with the authors about the best way to implement it. Very exciting! New design space for CtD! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />' 'Also, the build-a-kith stretch goal was pretty much directly inspired by the build-you-own-fae system in DA:F.' <br /> <br /> 17. Will Dauntain get attention in the first product? 'Yes, and I'm really excited about them (which is kind of ironic, I guess). Look for an excerpt on the KS soon.'<br /> <br /> 18. 'Oaths do indeed get attention and systems, but I'm not that far in the book yet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />'<br /> <br /> 19. Will there still be Arts, such as Sovereign, Talecraft and Infusion, that are restricted to one kith? 'Not so much.' [From comments on this forum, we know some kith-specific Arts will become their own subsystems (perhaps Infusion, given the comments on nockers?), while others will no longer be restricted.]<br /> <br /> 20. Updates on the kiths? Yes. 'I think we'd do &quot;Lore of the Kith&quot; rather than separate books, though.'<br /> <br /> 21. Changes to boons and bans? 'Not sure yet; I'm not that far in the redlines. I'm sure that something will wind up getting changed.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 12-21-2015, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T13:47:05-08:00","id":789906,"title":"","content":"Thank you for this. I wasn't even aware they did an AMA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1